# ─── Connecting the front end to Adminium ────────────────────────────────────
#
# BOTH ARE READ AT BUILD TIME, not at run time. Vite inlines them into the
# bundle, so setting either after a build does nothing until the next one.
#
# Leave them empty and the app builds in DEMO mode: realistic sample data
# compiled into the JavaScript, with a demo dock for switching personas. That is
# what the adminium.dev demos serve. It is not what you want on your own domain
# — nothing in it can be edited, exported or kept.
#
# Set them for a STANDALONE deployment — the app on its own domain, talking back
# to an Adminium somewhere else. Mint the key in Studio -> Public API.
#
# (There is a third arrangement where Adminium serves the app itself and neither
# variable is needed, because the browser is already on Adminium's origin and
# uses your session. This repo does not build that yet -- client-portal is the
# only one that does.)
# The key is public by design (`adm_pub_`): it selects a scope, reads only what
# that scope lists, and is refused outside /api/v1/public. A secret `adm_sk_`
# key here would be a real leak.
VITE_ADMINIUM_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_ADMINIUM_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
